diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index f6eca78..f86e90c 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -48,6 +48,20 @@ Once you have one, set it in the `SECRET_KEY_BASE` environment variable:
 docker run --env SECRET_KEY_BASE=abcdefabcdef ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications
+
+Set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to the same Web Push VAPID key pair
+in both the web and background-job environments. Keep the private key secret and
+preserve the pair across deployments; existing browser subscriptions depend on it.
+Only the public key is sent to browsers. Without both keys, push notifications
+remain disabled and tray and email notifications continue to work.
+
+Push requires HTTPS (localhost is supported for development), a running job worker,
+and outbound HTTPS access to browsers' push services. Run database migrations as
+usual when upgrading. People can then enable push for each browser/device from
+**Notification Settings**. On iOS, install Fizzy on the Home Screen first.
+Turning notifications off affects only that user's registration on that device.
+
 #### SSL
 
 If you want the Fizzy container to handle its own SSL automatically, you just need to specify the domain name that you're running it on.
